.TH "dotnet-nuget-add-client-cert" "1" "2026-11-13" "" ".NET Documentation"
.hy
.SH dotnet nuget add client-cert
.PP
\f[B]This article applies to:\f[R] \[u2714]\[uFE0F] .NET Core 3.1.400 SDK and later versions
.SH NAME
.PP
dotnet-nuget-add-client-cert - Add a client certificate configuration for a NuGet package source.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet nuget add client-cert --package-source <SOURCE_NAME>
    --path <CERTIFICATE_PATH> [--password <PASSWORD>]
    [--store-password-in-clear-text] --configfile <FILE> [-f|--force]

dotnet nuget add client-cert --package-source <SOURCE_NAME>
    --find-value <VALUE> [--find-by <FIND_TYPE>]
    [--store-location <LOCATION>] [--store-name <STORE_NAME>]
    [--configfile <FILE>] [-f|--force]

dotnet nuget add client-cert -h|--help
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \f[V]dotnet nuget add client-cert\f[R] command adds a client certificate configuration to the \f[V]clientCertificates\f[R] section of your NuGet configuration files.
Use a client certificate to authenticate to an HTTPS package source that requires client certificate authentication.
.PP
First, configure the package source with dotnet nuget add source.
Then, associate a certificate with the source\[cq]s name, not its URL.
Choose one certificate source:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]File:\f[R] Use \f[V]--path\f[R] to specify a PKCS #12 (\f[V].pfx\f[R] or \f[V].p12\f[R]) file that contains the certificate and its private key.
Specify \f[V]--configfile\f[R] when you add a certificate from a file.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Certificate store:\f[R] Use \f[V]--find-value\f[R] to select a certificate from a certificate store.
By default, NuGet searches by thumbprint in the current user\[cq]s personal (\f[V]My\f[R]) store.
.PP
Don\[cq]t combine file options (\f[V]--path\f[R] and \f[V]--password\f[R]) with store options (\f[V]--store-location\f[R], \f[V]--store-name\f[R], \f[V]--find-by\f[R], and \f[V]--find-value\f[R]).
Certificate store availability depends on your operating system.
.PP
Each package source can have only one client certificate configuration.
If a configuration already exists for the source, the command fails.
To change an existing configuration, use dotnet nuget update client-cert.
.PP
Unless you specify \f[V]--force\f[R], NuGet checks that it can find and load the certificate before it saves the configuration.
The command doesn\[cq]t test authentication with the package source.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\f[B]\f[VB]--configfile <FILE>\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
The NuGet configuration file (\f[I]nuget.config\f[R]) to use.
If specified, only the settings from this file will be used.
If not specified, the hierarchy of configuration files from the current directory will be used.
For more information, see Common NuGet Configurations.
.PP
Required when you add a certificate from a file.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--find-by <FIND_TYPE>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
The certificate store search method.
Defaults to \f[V]Thumbprint\f[R].
Values are case-insensitive.
Use an X.509 find type \f[B]without\f[R] the \f[V]FindBy\f[R] prefix.
For example, use \f[V]SubjectName\f[R], not \f[V]FindBySubjectName\f[R].
.PP
Use one of these values: \f[V]Thumbprint\f[R], \f[V]SubjectName\f[R], \f[V]SubjectDistinguishedName\f[R], \f[V]IssuerName\f[R], \f[V]IssuerDistinguishedName\f[R], \f[V]SerialNumber\f[R], \f[V]TemplateName\f[R], \f[V]ApplicationPolicy\f[R], \f[V]CertificatePolicy\f[R], \f[V]Extension\f[R], \f[V]KeyUsage\f[R], or \f[V]SubjectKeyIdentifier\f[R].
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--find-value <VALUE>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
The value to search for in the certificate store, such as a certificate thumbprint or subject name.
Required for a certificate store configuration.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]-f|--force\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Saves the configuration even if NuGet can\[cq]t find or load the certificate.
Use this option to configure a certificate before it\[cq]s available.
This option doesn\[cq]t disable HTTPS server certificate validation.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\f[VB]-?|-h|--help\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Prints out a description of how to use the command.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]-s|--package-source <SOURCE_NAME>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
The name of the package source to associate with the certificate, as defined in the \f[V]packageSources\f[R] section of your NuGet configuration.
Required.
Specify the source name, not its URL.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--password <PASSWORD>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
The password for the certificate file, if needed.
Use only with a file configuration.
By default, NuGet encrypts the password before it saves it.
.RS
.PP
Password encryption is supported only on Windows.
Only the same user on the same machine can decrypt the password.
.RE
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--path <CERTIFICATE_PATH>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
The path to the certificate file.
Required for a file configuration.
.PP
To select a specific file, use an absolute path.
For a relative path, NuGet first checks the current working directory.
If the file isn\[cq]t there, NuGet checks the path relative to the directory that contains the NuGet configuration file.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--store-location <LOCATION>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
The certificate store location: \f[V]CurrentUser\f[R] or \f[V]LocalMachine\f[R].
Defaults to \f[V]CurrentUser\f[R].
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--store-name <STORE_NAME>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
The certificate store name.
Accepted values are \f[V]AddressBook\f[R], \f[V]AuthRoot\f[R], \f[V]CertificateAuthority\f[R], \f[V]Disallowed\f[R], \f[V]My\f[R], \f[V]Root\f[R], \f[V]TrustedPeople\f[R], and \f[V]TrustedPublisher\f[R].
Defaults to \f[V]My\f[R], the personal certificate store.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--store-password-in-clear-text\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Saves the certificate file password without encryption.
To save a password on a platform other than Windows, specify this option with \f[V]--password\f[R].
.RS
.PP
[!WARNING] Avoid clear-text passwords when possible.
Restrict access to configuration files that contain passwords, and don\[cq]t commit passwords or private keys to source control.
.RE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Before you run these examples, configure a package source named \f[V]Contoso\f[R] in \f[V]nuget.config\f[R] and obtain a client certificate for that source.
.IP \[bu] 2
Add a certificate from a file without a password:
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet nuget add client-cert --package-source Contoso --path .\[rs]client.pfx --configfile .\[rs]nuget.config
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Add a password-protected certificate file on Windows.
Replace \f[V]<CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD>\f[R] with the file\[cq]s password:
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet nuget add client-cert --package-source Contoso --path .\[rs]client.pfx --password <CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD> --configfile .\[rs]nuget.config
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Add a certificate from the current user\[cq]s personal store.
Replace \f[V]<CERTIFICATE_THUMBPRINT>\f[R] with the certificate\[cq]s thumbprint:
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet nuget add client-cert --package-source Contoso --find-value <CERTIFICATE_THUMBPRINT> --configfile .\[rs]nuget.config
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Add a certificate from the current user\[cq]s personal store by subject name:
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet nuget add client-cert --package-source Contoso --store-location CurrentUser --store-name My --find-by SubjectName --find-value \[dq]Contoso NuGet client\[dq] --configfile .\[rs]nuget.config
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Each example adds a configuration for the same source.
Remove the existing configuration before you try another example.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \[bu] 2
dotnet nuget list client-cert
.IP \[bu] 2
dotnet nuget remove client-cert
.IP \[bu] 2
dotnet nuget update client-cert
